  "note": "Whole-council election of the Portstewart Urban District Council, polled 15 May 1936 (the January 1935 round having been deferred by the Local Government Act (Northern Ireland) 1934). Fifteen candidates stood for twelve seats. The Belfast Telegraph prints the result and the defeated candidates. Eight new councillors; the four retiring members who offered themselves were re-elected."
